Make the following AOT-compatibility fixes in the project at `/tmp/sv-e000e7f7afe64137947621ae9d640beb/before/`. Do NOT run any builds. Just make the edits.

## 1. ArmOperation.cs
Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]` annotation to the generic type parameter `T` in:
- `Rehydrate<T>` method (line 44): add `where T : notnull` becomes a constraint but also annotate. Actually the constraint is `where T : notnull`. Change both Rehydrate<T> and RehydrateAsync<T> to use a private helper with annotation.

Actually, the fix is to add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to `T` in the `IsResource<T>()` method, since that's where `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` are called.

Since `IsResource<T>` is private, the annotation on `T` needs to flow from callers. The callers are `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>` which are public methods. So you need to:

1. Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` at the top (it's not already there)
2. Change `IsResource<T>()` to: `private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull`
3. Change `Rehydrate<T>` (line 44) to: `public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull`
4. Change `RehydrateAsync<T>` (line 82) to: `public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, RehydrationToken rehydrationToken, ArmClientOptions options = null) where T : notnull`

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs
The class `GenericOperationSource<T>` uses `typeof(T)` in `ModelReaderWriter.Read` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`.

1. Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` (it's already there actually)
2. Change the class declaration to: `internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>`

## 3. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs
The `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` method calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` which is marked with `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. 

Add attributes to the method:
```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types.")]
public static IAzureClientBuilder<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions> AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>(this TBuilder builder, TConfiguration configuration)
```

The file already has `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;`.

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs
Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` on line 80 with manual JSON serialization. The struct has properties: Endpoint (Uri), Audience (string), DefaultScope (string).

Change line 80 from:
```csharp
public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);
```
to:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\",\"DefaultScope\":\"{DefaultScope}\"}}";
}
```

Wait actually that's fragile. Use Utf8JsonWriter instead:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    using var stream = new System.IO.MemoryStream();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(stream))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteString("DefaultScope", DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(stream.ToArray());
}
```

Add `using System.IO;` and `using System.Text;` if not present. Remove `using System.Text.Json;` if no longer needed. Actually wait, `Utf8JsonWriter` is in `System.Text.Json`, so keep that using.

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs
Replace `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` on line 52 with manual parsing using JsonDocument.

Change:
```csharp
var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
```
to:
```csharp
using var profileDoc = JsonDocument.Parse(span.ToArray());
var allProfile = new Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>();
foreach (var outerProp in profileDoc.RootElement.EnumerateObject())
{
